 To find the cross product of two vectors $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} d \\ e \\ f \end{pmatrix}$, we use the formula:
\[
\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \\ c \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} d \\ e \\ f \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} be - cf \\ cd - af \\ ad - be \end{pmatrix}
\]
Applying this to our vectors $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 4 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}$, we get:
\begin{align*}
a &= 1, & b &= -1, & c &= 2, \\
d &= 3, & e &= 4, & f &= -5.
\end{align*}
Substituting these values into the formula, we find the cross product to be:
\begin{align*}
\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 4 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} (-1)(-5) - (2)(4) \\ (2)(3) - (1)(-5) \\ (1)(4) - (-1)(3) \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 5 - 8 \\ 6 + 5 \\ 4 + 3 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 11 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
